# Project Coding Standards

## Code Comments
- DO NOT add comments to code files
- Code should be self-explanatory through clear naming and structure
- Remove any existing comments when editing files

## Import Statements
- ALWAYS use `@/*` path aliases instead of relative paths (e.g., `../../` or `./`)
- Use `@/` prefix for all imports from the src directory
- Use `@/messages/*` for message files
- Never use relative imports like `../` or `./` in import statements
- Update any existing relative imports to use `@/*` aliases

## Code Quality & Deployment
- Always write production-ready code that is safe to deploy
- Double-check all code before finalizing changes
- Ensure code is tested and follows best practices

## Feature Development
- When adding features, design them to be easily expandable and maintainable
- Follow all best practices for scalability and maintainability
- Use modular architecture and separation of concerns
- Write reusable, composable components and functions
- Follow SOLID principles and design patterns where appropriate

## Code Organization & Architecture
- Always place code in the best location following industry standards and design patterns
- Follow established architectural patterns (e.g., feature-based, domain-driven, layered architecture)
- Organize code by feature/domain rather than by file type when appropriate
- Keep related code together and maintain clear separation of concerns
- Place shared utilities in appropriate shared directories
- Place feature-specific code in feature-specific directories
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions and best practices
- Maintain consistent folder structure and naming conventions throughout the application

